One pass over the entries appends each table to an array keyed by its owner (or `"unassigned"`), then each array is sorted. O(n log n) time for the sorts, O(n) space. Sorting the table names first and then grouping (so arrays come out sorted) is also fine.

def tables_by_owner(owners):
    groups = {}
    for table, owner in owners.items():
        key = owner if owner is not None else "unassigned"
